cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite this release record.
title: "Kepler: 100.00 at Median-Human-or-Better Action Efficiency on Every ARC-AGI-3 Public Level"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Wensen
    alias: Cveinnt
    email: contact@wensenwu.com
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Cveinnt/kepler"
url: "https://kepler-harness.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Kepler is an open-source agent harness that reaches a server-verified exact
  100.00 RHAE on all 25 public ARC-AGI-3 games with one frozen Claude Opus 5
  configuration and no score-conditioned reruns. Every level meets or exceeds
  median-human action efficiency. The board uses 7,292 scored actions and costs
  $1,568.50 at current API list-equivalent rates. The release includes complete
  provider-side resource accounting, score-lineage tools, an enforced
  zero-game-priors check, negative results, and incident reports for two
  integrity failures caught in our own experiments. The full trace dataset is
  a required companion artifact and remains marked pending until its public URL
  appears in release.json.
keywords:
  - ARC-AGI-3
  - world models
  - LLM agents
  - agent evaluation
